# Page CSS and JS belong in assets, not in the HTML

GOV.UK Prototype Kit pages should stay readable. Put **markup and Nunjucks in the HTML file**. Put **styles and behaviour in asset files** once either is more than a short paragraph (roughly more than ~15 lines).

## What can stay in the HTML

- Server data as JSON script tags (Nunjucks cannot run inside a static `.js` file)
- Third-party / plugin `<link>` and `<script>` tags

Do **not** use `style=""` in templates. Put the CSS in the page Sass file and toggle a class with Nunjucks or JS (`app-js-hidden`, `hidden`, or a named layout class). JS that already sets `style.display` can keep doing that — it overrides the class.

## CSS

1. Create `app/assets/sass/<journey>-<page>.scss` (example: `sfi-grasslands-v2-select-actions.scss`)
2. Link it from the page as `/public/stylesheets/<filename>.css` (after plugin CSS if you override it)
3. Do **not** `@import` page styles into `application.scss` — that file runs on every page

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/stylesheets/sfi-grasslands-v2-select-actions.css">
```

## JavaScript

1. Create `app/assets/javascripts/<journey>-<page>.js`
2. Include it from `{% block pageScripts %}` as `/public/javascripts/<filename>.js`
3. Load it **after** shared scripts it depends on
4. Do **not** add page-specific behaviour to `application.js`

```html
<script id="session-data" type="application/json">{{ data['parcelSelectionsData'] | safe }}</script>
<script src="/public/javascripts/sfi-grasslands-v2-select-actions.js"></script>
```

## New asset files

- Start with a short comment saying which page loads the file
- Prefer an IIFE for new JS so you do not leak globals (do not wrap existing extracted files unless asked)
- Do not copy large inline `<style>` or `<script>` blocks into new pages; extract first
